=== QCA cells as an entangling gate ===

1. Ground-state entanglement vs J/g ratio (g = 0.1):

   J/g         E0     S(A)        C    F_GHZ
----------------------------------------------
   0.1   -0.20025   0.0052   0.0364   0.5250
   0.5   -0.20616   0.0776   0.1047   0.6213
   1.0   -0.22361   0.2066   0.1848   0.7236
   2.0   -0.28284   0.4165   0.3257   0.8536
   5.0   -0.53852   0.6225   0.5504   0.9642
  10.0   -1.01980   0.6738   0.6829   0.9903
  20.0   -2.00998   0.6882   0.7765   0.9975

2. Adiabatic gate: turn on g=0.1 with J=1.0 over T=50:
   S(A)     = 0.1231
   C        = 0.0180
   F_GHZ    = 0.4952

3. Fast quench (T=1) vs slow adiabatic (T=50):
   T =    1.0   S = 0.0000   C = 0.0000
   T =    5.0   S = 0.0024   C = 0.0000
   T =   20.0   S = 0.0276   C = 0.0000
   T =   50.0   S = 0.1231   C = 0.0180
   T =  200.0   S = 0.6541   C = 0.5494

Interpretation:
  J/g > 5 : near-maximal entanglement, C -> 1, S -> ln 2
  J/g < 1 : product state, C -> 0, S -> 0
  Adiabatic ramp populates the cat state on demand.
  A QCA wire built from J/g > 5 cells is a CHAIN OF
  NATIVE 2-QUBIT ENTANGLING GATES.
